{"availability":"available","full":"joseluismontezamilian12-rgb/merma-ai","name":"merma-ai","description":"Inventory & shrinkage control for food retail — order-cycle-aware recommendations from real consumption history. Piloted at the store I managed (sanitized demo data). React + Vite, zero backend","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-03T05:13:45Z","updated":"2026-09-26T23:26:10Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://joseluismontezamilian12-rgb.github.io/merma-ai/","topics":["food-retail","github-pages","inventory-management","localstorage","loss-prevention","react","spa","vite"],"demo":"https://joseluismontezamilian12-rgb.github.io/merma-ai/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:40.670Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:40.670Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:40.670Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T22:39:40.670Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["React SPA that turns paper-and-memory store ordering into data. I built it as a store manager to solve my own problem: inaccurate orders that ended up as shrinkage (merma) — expired product thrown away, money lost.","Field-tested: I piloted this at the fast-casual store I managed in Lima, loaded with the store's real catalog (78 SKUs with official portioning and shelf life), three real weekly orders and a real stock-exit record, to cross-check warehouse stock, orders and shrinkage before every order day. This public repo ships a sanitized demo dataset — the original store data is confidential and stays out of version control.","The project started as an AI-assisted prototype and the name stuck at the store. The version I actually ran the pilot with — this one — is deliberately rule-based: the operation needed explainable numbers a store team could trust and argue with, not a black box. (An LLM layer for parsing unstructured inventory logs is the natural next iteration.)"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/joseluismontezamilian12-rgb/merma-ai/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4a170d8910ecbc3d023605f53357a4a13416c62f3c90cc9c993bed98924ff950","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:40.824Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:40.824Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"React SPA that turns paper-and-memory store ordering into data. I built it as a store manager to solve my own problem: inaccurate orders that ended up as shrinkage (merma) — expired product thrown away, money lost.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/joseluismontezamilian12-rgb/merma-ai/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"The operation needed \"an Excel, but as a web page\" — deliberately no servers, no accounts, no setup.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/joseluismontezamilian12-rgb/merma-ai/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"4a170d8910ecbc3d023605f53357a4a13416c62f3c90cc9c993bed98924ff950","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/joseluismontezamilian12-rgb/merma-ai/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:40.824Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-26T23:26:10Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/joseluismontezamilian12-rgb/merma-ai/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:40.825Z","hash":"4a170d8910ecbc3d023605f53357a4a13416c62f3c90cc9c993bed98924ff950","originalBytes":3055,"storedBytes":3055,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["store","shrinkage","order","real","orders","license","localstorage","merma","npm","product","react","run","stock-exit","build","calendar","catalog","consumption","day.","days","deliberately","demo","dev","each","fri","github","inventory","life","lima","name","needed","next","operation","ordered","original","per","prototype","records","shelf","stock","thu","tue","version","a.k.a.","accounts","across","actually","ai-assisted","alerts.","always","api","app","argue","artifacts","assi